menu "FlightWall owned firmware (skeleton)"

config FW_TLS_ARENA_BYTES
    int "TLS arena size (bytes), reserved statically at boot"
    range 32768 65536
    default 49152
    help
        Fixed .bss arena for the source-built TLS engine; it never falls back to
        the system heap. 49152 is the smallest size verified against the real
        route service on the desktop. Reserving it statically means the size
        report counts it and runtime fragmentation cannot deny it later.

config FW_PROBE_TASK_STACK
    int "Network probe task stack (bytes)"
    range 6144 16384
    default 10240
    help
        TLS handshakes (ECDHE + certificate verification) are stack-hungry.
        The probe reports this task's high-water mark so the final value can be
        set from measurement.

config FW_PROBE_ROUNDS
    int "Route requests per probe run"
    range 1 20
    default 3
    help
        Several identical requests show whether heap returns to the same level
        after each, i.e. whether anything leaks per connection.

config FW_PROBE_HOST
    string "Route service host"
    default "api.adsbdb.com"

config FW_PROBE_PATH
    string "Route service path (public test callsign, not owner data)"
    default "/v0/callsign/DAL42"

config FW_PENDING_RESTART_S
    int "Restart after N seconds when running unconfirmed (pending) image"
    range 30 600
    default 240
    help
        If this image was installed as a pending OTA update, it never confirms
        itself. After the probe (or this deadline), it restarts so the
        installed bootloader marks it ABORTED and returns to the previous,
        known-good firmware.

config FW_DISPLAY_ENABLE
    bool "Drive the HUB75 panels"
    default y
    help
        Starts the panel driver with the configuration recovered from the vendor
        firmware (PANEL.md) and shows a test pattern while the network probe runs.

config FW_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS
    int "Panel brightness (0-255)"
    range 1 255
    default 40
    help
        The owner normally runs the panels at about 15%. A low value keeps
        supply current modest during tests; the vendor uses 160 only briefly.

config FW_PROBE
    bool "Run the start-up network probe (skeleton measurement)"
    default y
    help
        Three TLS route requests once online, measuring heap and stack. A
        measurement for test builds; keepable builds leave it out.

config FW_KEEPABLE
    bool "Keepable build: may confirm itself when the owner asks"
    default n
    help
        Off (test builds): the update service refuses POST /v1/firmware/confirm,
        so an installed image always rolls back to the previous firmware. On:
        the owner's confirmation (the desk sends it after an upload) keeps the
        image if it is healthy (online, panel running); a kept image no longer
        restarts at the end of the view window. See UPDATES.md.

config FW_WIFI_FAIL_ATTEMPTS
    int "Test: make the first N connection attempts fail"
    range 0 20
    default 0
    help
        Board test of the failure path (SETUP.md "Wi-Fi failure and
        reconnect"): the first N attempts look for a network that does not
        exist instead of a saved one, so boot fails, setup mode starts and the
        retries take over. Nothing is written. 0 = off.

config FW_WIFI_DROP_AFTER_S
    int "Test: drop Wi-Fi once, N seconds after first getting online"
    range 0 570
    default 0
    help
        Board test of losing the network: disconnects once, N seconds after
        the board first came online, and fails the next FW_WIFI_DROP_FAILS
        attempts, so the "Lost connection" messages and retries show. 0 = off.

config FW_WIFI_DROP_FAILS
    int "Test: attempts that fail after the drop"
    range 0 20
    default 3

config FW_SETUP_SAVE
    bool "Save provisioned Wi-Fi credentials like stock, then restart"
    default n
    help
        After a successful test join, store the station config the way the
        stock firmware does (Arduino WiFi.begin, persistent: the Wi-Fi driver's
        own NVS storage), but only when it differs from the stored one, mark
        the identity provisioned if it is not, put the network first in
        stock's saved list, and restart after 5 s. These are the owned
        firmware's only NVS writes. Off: test-join only, nothing saved.

config FW_SETUP_HTTPS
    bool "Also serve the stock HTTPS setup endpoints (vendor app)"
    default n
    help
        Adds the stock-compatible HTTPS server on 443 with the board's identity
        certificate, so the vendor app's pinned fingerprint matches, and the
        vendor QR page. Only useful for setting up the owned firmware with the
        vendor app; stock keeps its own setup either way. About 160 KB of flash.

config FW_SAFE_MODE_CRASHES
    int "Start in safe mode after this many crashes in a row (0 = never)"
    range 0 10
    default 3
    help
        Consecutive panic or watchdog resets, counted in RTC memory. Safe mode
        starts only Wi-Fi and the update service (UPDATES.md "Safe mode").

config FW_SAFE_MODE_HEALTHY_S
    int "Seconds of running that clear the crash count"
    range 30 3600
    default 120

config FW_SAFE_MODE_TEST
    bool "Test build: always start in safe mode"
    default n
    help
        Only to check safe mode on the board with a pending test image (which
        still rolls back by itself).

config FW_VIEW_SECONDS
    int "Keep a pending image up at least N seconds after boot"
    range 0 570
    default 180
    help
        Gives time to look at the panel test pattern before the unconfirmed
        image restarts and the bootloader rolls back. Must stay below
        FW_PENDING_RESTART_S, the hard deadline.

endmenu
